diagnosis_text:
Current reachability between hosts is healthy (pc_0_0 → pc_0_1 ping succeeds), but the CLOS fabric is not load-balancing as expected. The affected component is the BGP ECMP policy on the leafs and the super-spine. Mechanism: FRR is selecting only a single “best” eBGP path because ECMP is not enabled; this forces all inter-leaf traffic to traverse one spine, matching the “squeezed down one road” observation. Evidence: on leaf_router_0_0, “show ip bgp 10.0.1.0/24” shows two paths via 172.16.0.4 and 172.16.0.8, but “show ip route” installs only one next-hop (via 172.16.0.4). Similarly, leaf_router_0_1 prefers only 172.16.0.6 for 10.0.0.0/24. On super_spine_router_0, both 1
